    <statement><p>Find the second partial derivatives of the function <m>\displaystyle f(x,y) = x^{6}y^5+6 x^{5}y.</m></p>
<p><alert> 1.</alert> <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial x^2} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> 2.</alert> <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial y \partial x} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert> 3.</alert> <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial x \partial y} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><alert> 4.</alert> <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial y^2} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6\cdot 5x^{4}y^{5}+6\cdot 5\cdot 4x^{6-3}y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cdot 6x^{5}y^{4}+6\cdot 5x^{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cdot 6x^{5}y^{4}+6\cdot 5x^{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>20x^{6}y^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
